      "body_html": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Well, later I will create a PR to add all deleted code back, in <code class=\"notranslate\">/* */</code> comment.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For this I had an idea:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When anyone modifies the exec code they should declare a file like</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-toml notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"[[anchor]]\ngit = &quot;https://github.com/asterinas/asterinas.git&quot;\ntag = &quot;0.16.0&quot;\npath = &quot;ostd/src/mm/vm_space.rs&quot;\n\n[functions.verified]\nname = &quot;VmSpace::cursor_mut&quot;\nhow = &quot;transcribe&quot;\n\n[functions.unsurpported]\nname = &quot;VmSpace::activate&quot;\nreason = &quot;lack-hardware-modelling&quot;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">[[<span class=\"pl-en\">anchor</span>]]\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">git</span> = <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>https://github.com/asterinas/asterinas.git<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">tag</span> = <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>0.16.0<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">path</span> = <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>ostd/src/mm/vm_space.rs<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>\n\n[<span class=\"pl-en\">functions</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">verified</span>]\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">name</span> = <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>VmSpace::cursor_mut<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">how</span> = <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>transcribe<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>\n\n[<span class=\"pl-en\">functions</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">unsurpported</span>]\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">name</span> = <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>VmSpace::activate<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">reason</span> = <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>lack-hardware-modelling<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">and we can use LLM to design a tool to check if anything is left undeclared and if there is any mismatches in the function signature, declaration, etc.</p>",
      "body_text": "Well, later I will create a PR to add all deleted code back, in /* */ comment.\n\nFor this I had an idea:\nWhen anyone modifies the exec code they should declare a file like\n[[anchor]]\ngit = \"https://github.com/asterinas/asterinas.git\"\ntag = \"0.16.0\"\npath = \"ostd/src/mm/vm_space.rs\"\n\n[functions.verified]\nname = \"VmSpace::cursor_mut\"\nhow = \"transcribe\"\n\n[functions.unsurpported]\nname = \"VmSpace::activate\"\nreason = \"lack-hardware-modelling\"\nand we can use LLM to design a tool to check if anything is left undeclared and if there is any mismatches in the function signature, declaration, etc.",
      "body": "> Well, later I will create a PR to add all deleted code back, in `/* */` comment.\r\n\r\nFor this I had an idea:\r\n\r\nWhen anyone modifies the exec code they should declare a file like\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[[anchor]]\r\ngit = \"https://github.com/asterinas/asterinas.git\"\r\ntag = \"0.16.0\"\r\npath = \"ostd/src/mm/vm_space.rs\"\r\n\r\n[functions.verified]\r\nname = \"VmSpace::cursor_mut\"\r\nhow = \"transcribe\"\r\n\r\n[functions.unsurpported]\r\nname = \"VmSpace::activate\"\r\nreason = \"lack-hardware-modelling\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nand we can use LLM to design a tool to check if anything is left undeclared and if there is any mismatches in the function signature, declaration, etc.",
